design.data_model:
// game.ts holds only rules and data. The catalogue, medals and unlocks go in a new src/stages.ts (pure, tested), and localStorage progress in src/progress.ts (pure core plus a thin storage wrapper).

```ts
// game.ts
export const THAW = -7, SNOW = -5, FRIEND = -6;  // with XBLOCK -1, CAPSULE -2, CLEAR -3
export interface LevelDef {
  colors: number; xChance: number; capsuleGuard: number;
  airDrain: number; wobble: number; fallSpeed: number;
  capsuleMul?: number;        // Aurora: irregular supply
  regulationTime?: number;    // s per 100m -> time bonus
  thawChance?: number; thawTime?: number;
  snowChance?: number;
  avalancheSpeed?: number;    // rows/s
  perSwing?: number;          // swing-mode air per hit
}
export type AirRule =
  | { kind: 'time' }
  | { kind: 'swing'; xBreakAir: number; crushAir: number; targetSwings: number };
export interface StageDef {
  id: string;
  cols: number;                 // 7 | 9 | 11
  levels: LevelDef[];           // fixed part; depth = levels.length*100 unless endless
  endless?: (n: number) => LevelDef;  // level n >= levels.length+1
  capsuleChance: number;        // per cell, before capsuleMul
  capsuleAir?: number;          // default AIR_CAPSULE (23)
  lives?: number;               // default START_LIVES; endless = 1
  extendScores?: number[];      // default EXTEND_SCORES; [] in endless
  seed?: number;                // fixed course seed (UI may override with Random)
  air: AirRule;
  rules: {
    friends?: { xPerFriend: number; points: number; lifeEvery: number };
    avalanche?: { start: number; resetGap: number; capsulePush: number };
  };
}
export interface RunStats { swings: number; livesLost: number; maxChain: number; maxPop: number;
  meltChains: number; friends: number; minAir: number; capsules: number; levelStart: number; }
export interface RunResult { stageId: string; won: boolean; depth: number; score: number;
  time: number; stats: RunStats; seeded: boolean; }
export function createGame(seed = stage.seed ?? Date.now(), stage = DEFAULT_STAGE): Game
export function runResult(g: Game, seeded: boolean): RunResult
```
How createGame uses it: cols = stage.cols. g.levels = [...stage.levels]. rows = SKY_ROWS + g.levels.length*100. g.rng = seed. generateRows(g, 1, L) draws per cell in this order: capsule (capsuleChance*capsuleMul), then X (odd rows), then thaw, then snow, then neighbour-colour bias, then random colour. CLEAR rows at each 100m. Capsule guard pass. lives = stage.lives ?? 3. air = 100. avalanche = rules.avalanche ? SKY_ROWS-1-start : null. xPopped = 0. stats zeroed. During play: update() branches on air.kind, and tick() runs the thaw timers, avalanche wipe/catch and endless append, each only when its data is present. A DEFAULT_STAGE with cols 9, air time and rules {} must reproduce today's game exactly.

```ts
// stages.ts
export type MedalTier = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3;          // none/bronze/silver/gold
export interface MedalRule { tier: 1|2|3; text_ko: string; test: (r: RunResult) => boolean; }
export type Unlock = { kind: 'open' } | { kind: 'cleared'; ids: string[] };
export interface StageMeta { def: StageDef; nameKo: string; blurbKo: string; mechanicKo: string;
  theme: string; unlock: Unlock; medals: MedalRule[]; scenery: string[] /* per-100m backdrop ids */ }
export const STAGES: StageMeta[];               // ordered 1..8
export function medalFor(meta: StageMeta, r: RunResult): MedalTier;  // highest tier whose test passes; each tier also requires the lower ones
export function isUnlocked(meta: StageMeta, p: Progress): boolean;
// progress.ts
export interface StageRecord { medal: MedalTier; cleared: boolean; bestScore: number;
  bestDepth: number; bestTime: number | null; bestSwings?: number; plays: number; }
export interface Progress { v: 1; stages: Record<string, StageRecord>; lastStage?: string; random?: boolean; }
export function recordRun(p: Progress, r: RunResult): { progress: Progress; medal: MedalTier;
  newBest: string[]; unlocked: string[] };   // pure: returns a new Progress
export function loadProgress(): Progress;    // try/catch, 'dig-down:progress:v1'; migrates 'dig-down:best' into frozen-lake
export function saveProgress(p: Progress): void;
```
Random-seed runs earn medals and unlocks. Seeded best scores and times are kept apart (`bestScore` only counts seeded runs) so route records stay comparable. This is an open question.
